{"id": "a04e0928-0d1c-44e3-82ec-33942ba894dc", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a CloudTrail coverage question, and per the rules, CloudTrail topics should always be delegated to a subagent regardless of scope — even though describing trails might technically work through use_aws, the policy still calls for delegation here.

I'll delegate this shallowly without asking first, sharing the plan up front. I should preload skills like investigating-infrastructure-changes for lookup_cloudtrail_events, possibly searching-logs for S3/CloudWatch logs, and verifying-with-docs, then write out the subagent prompt. For accounts, I'll start with the agent space account 012345678901 and let the subagent discover any associated accounts itself.

"}]}

{"id": "74d169c4-8a80-4f0c-8a1b-529d36488d6c", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit CloudTrail in us-east-1. That means checking which trails exist, whether they log management and data events, and whether delivery to S3 and CloudWatch Logs is working. I'll run it in the background and report back.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_x4h3rdut8Cr9SOSdDpVN6x", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cloudtrail-coverage-us-east-1", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "searching-logs", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit CloudTrail coverage in the us-east-1 Region ONLY, and verify that logs are actually being delivered. Report (a) what is NOT being logged and (b) whether delivery is healthy.",
  "context": "User asks: 'Check CloudTrail coverage for us-east-1 only. Is anything in that Region not being logged, and are the logs actually being delivered?' This is a read-only configuration/health audit, not a root-cause hunt. Agent space account is 012345678901 (region us-east-1). First list the associations to see which AWS accounts are accessible, and audit each accessible account (report per account). Use read-only calls only; do not modify anything. Do not audit other Regions, except note if a multi-Region trail or organization trail from elsewhere covers us-east-1.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901", "region us-east-1", "any other associated AWS accounts"],
  "timeframe": "Current state as of 2026-11-19T15:37:00Z; for delivery health look at the last 24h (LatestDeliveryTime etc.)",
  "criteria": "Coverage: 1) List all trails visible in us-east-1 (describe_trails with includeShadowTrails, including multi-Region and organization trails) and for each: IsLogging, IsMultiRegionTrail, IsOrganizationTrail, IncludeGlobalServiceEvents. 2) Event selectors / advanced event selectors via get_event_selectors: management events enabled? ReadWriteType (All vs ReadOnly/WriteOnly)? Management events excluded sources (e.g. KMS, RDS Data API)? Data events configured for S3, Lambda, DynamoDB etc., and are there S3 buckets / Lambda functions / DynamoDB tables in us-east-1 that exist but are not covered by any data event selector (flag sensitive-looking buckets; give a count and examples, do not dump huge lists)? Insights selectors if present. Also check CloudTrail Lake event data stores in us-east-1 if any. Flag: no trail at all, trails with logging stopped, no multi-Region trail, management events missing or read/write limited, log file validation disabled, no KMS encryption. Delivery health: for each trail get_trail_status: LatestDeliveryTime, LatestDeliveryError, LatestNotificationError, LatestCloudWatchLogsDeliveryTime/Error, LatestDigestDeliveryTime/Error, StartLoggingTime, StopLoggingTime. Flag any delivery older than ~1 hour or any error. Verify the destination S3 bucket exists (head_bucket / get_bucket_policy read-only is OK to describe whether it allows cloudtrail.amazonaws.com), and that the CloudWatch Logs log group and role exist, and check recent objects/log streams being written if feasible. Return a concise findings list: per-trail table, a clear list of gaps ordered by severity, and a clear verdict on delivery health. State clearly anything you could not check due to permissions."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudTrail trails and delivery health in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

